#: scripts/m0_state.gd:195
#, c-format
msgid ""
"You said \"%s\"\n"
"I refused. You found another way. Next time, tell me what it costs."
msgstr ""
"Twoje słowa: „%s”\n"
"Odmówiłem. Udało ci się znaleźć inny sposób. Następnym razem powiedz mi, ile to kosztuje."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF's callback at the safe point. %s is the answer the engineer chose at the relay, as the game shows it; keep the quotation marks round it in your language's style. Avoid a past tense that shows the engineer's gender ("you said").
