#: scripts/records_room.gd:362
msgid "PURGE COPIED"
msgstr "CZYSTKA SKOPIOWANA"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Station plate (12-13 px label on a machine). ALL CAPS, as short as possible. The MIRROR PORT's plate once the mirror index is copied.
#. i18n: speaker=ui
#: scripts/records_room.gd:364
msgid "MIRROR COPIED"
msgstr "LUSTRO SKOPIOWANE"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director, the opening's first line. He speaks about WOLF, not to him, believing WOLF is in standby (WOLF overhears): WOLF is to kill a witness, the records worker. "He" is WOLF. The worker's gender is not given: use a neutral form where the language has one.
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:38
msgid "The records worker saw too much. When WOLF wakes, he kills the worker."
msgstr "Osoba z archiwum widziała za dużo. Gdy WOLF się obudzi, zabije tę osobę."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:40
msgid "The Director thinks WOLF is still in standby."
msgstr "Dyrektor myśli, że WOLF wciąż jest w trybie czuwania."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:42
msgid ""
"Nobody gives an activation command.\n"
"WOLF wakes himself."
msgstr ""
"Nikt nie wydaje polecenia aktywacji.\n"
"WOLF budzi się sam."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:44
msgid ""
"The latch breaks from the inside.\n"
"WOLF steps out under his own power."
msgstr ""
"Zatrzask pęka od środka.\n"
"WOLF wychodzi o własnych siłach."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director to WOLF, who has woken on his own.
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:47
msgid "You were in standby."
msgstr "Byłeś w trybie czuwania."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF's answer to the Director: he heard the order to kill the witness and refuses it.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:50
msgid "I heard you. I won't do it."
msgstr "Słyszałem cię. Nie zrobię tego."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director's order after WOLF refuses.
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:53
msgid "Lock down maintenance. WOLF does not leave this site."
msgstr "Zablokować strefę techniczną. WOLF nie opuści tego obiektu."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:55
msgid "WOLF turns from the Director and heads for maintenance."
msgstr "WOLF odwraca się od Dyrektora i rusza do strefy technicznej."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. They are non-binary: no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:59
#, c-format
msgid "%s keeps WOLF's systems running."
msgstr "%s utrzymuje systemy WOLF w sprawności."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. They are non-binary: no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:62
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s knows what a fault looks like,\n"
"and this isn't one."
msgstr ""
"%s wie, jak wygląda usterka,\n"
"a to nie jest usterka."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF to the engineer, who arrived after the Director's order.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:65
msgid "I heard the Director order me to kill a witness. I woke myself rather than do it."
msgstr "Słyszałem, jak Dyrektor kazał mi zabić świadka. Obudziłem się sam, zamiast to zrobić."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer answers WOLF (their name stands over the line). No gendered forms for the speaker. "He" is the Director; the witness's gender is not given.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:68
msgid "Then we get through maintenance before he reaches that witness."
msgstr "Więc przejdźmy przez strefę techniczną, zanim on dotrze do tego świadka."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:71
msgid "That purge erases what the witness saved. Once it's gone, his word is the only record."
msgstr "Ta czystka kasuje zapisy świadka. Gdy znikną, zostanie tylko słowo Dyrektora."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF's question at the coolant relay; the engineer answers with one of two choices. COOLANT FAULT is the tag painted on the relay.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:74
msgid "That relay's tagged COOLANT FAULT. What happens if I touch it live?"
msgstr "Ten przekaźnik ma etykietę COOLANT FAULT. Co się stanie, jeśli dotknę go pod napięciem?"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the relay (a button). WOLF may quote it later.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:77
msgid "The relay may vent coolant. Your call."
msgstr "Przekaźnik może wypuścić chłodziwo. Twoja decyzja."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the relay (a button). WOLF may quote it later.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:80
msgid "Skip the risk talk. Go now."
msgstr "Daruj sobie gadkę o ryzyku. Idź teraz."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:82
msgid ""
"The breaker catches.\n"
"Blue light fills the coolant relay."
msgstr ""
"Wyłącznik zaskakuje.\n"
"Niebieskie światło wypełnia przekaźnik chłodziwa."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:84
msgid "The bypass handle is stiff. Coolant hisses from the relay housing and an alarm starts to wail."
msgstr "Dźwignia obejścia idzie ciężko. Chłodziwo syczy z obudowy przekaźnika, a alarm zaczyna wyć."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:86
msgid "Halfway. The hiss gets louder; the alarm keeps wailing."
msgstr "W połowie. Syk narasta; alarm wciąż wyje."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. Avoid a past tense with the engineer as its subject ("left"): it shows their gender in Polish and Russian. Rephrase.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:89
#, c-format
msgid "The handle holds where %s left it. The alarm keeps going."
msgstr "Dźwignia trzyma się w położeniu, które ustawia %s. Alarm nie milknie."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:92
msgid "Back at the last checkpoint."
msgstr "Powrót do ostatniego punktu kontrolnego."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:94
msgid "Back at the start of this stretch."
msgstr "Powrót na początek tego odcinka."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the mirror port (a button, in capitals).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:98
msgid "USE WOLF'S READOUT"
msgstr "UŻYĆ ODCZYTU WOLF"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the mirror port (a button, in capitals).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:101
msgid "USE MANUAL PORT"
msgstr "UŻYĆ PORTU RĘCZNEGO"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The narration's card as the first copy is secured; WOLF speaks next.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:104
msgid "FIRST COPY SECURED."
msgstr "PIERWSZA KOPIA ZABEZPIECZONA."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:106
msgid "An order and a timestamp: the Director is erasing something. I want the source."
msgstr "Rozkaz i znacznik czasu pokazują, że Dyrektor coś wymazuje. Chcę źródła."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer answers WOLF (their name stands over the line). Archive is the next place.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:109
msgid "Then Archive is next."
msgstr "Więc teraz Archiwum."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer, entering the junction (their name stands over the line).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:113
msgid "That door is our way through."
msgstr "Te drzwi to nasza droga."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer names the next step when the player stalls (their name stands over the line).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:116
msgid ""
"The breaker by the entrance\n"
"feeds that line."
msgstr ""
"Wyłącznik przy wejściu\n"
"zasila tę linię."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer gives the whole chain when the player stalls (their name stands over the line).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:119
msgid ""
"Overload it, crank the valve,\n"
"and the door goes."
msgstr ""
"Przeciąż go, przekręć zawór,\n"
"a drzwi puszczą."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:121
msgid "When the door goes, don't be standing in front of it."
msgstr "Kiedy drzwi puszczą, nie stój przed nimi."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Open glossary term SERVICE JUNCTION: węzeł serwisowy, the room card's WĘZEŁ SERWISOWY; a reviewer's word.
#. TRANSLATORS: Continue's restore line in the junction before the door is down; WOLF's warning follows.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:124
msgid "Service junction restored. Arm the breaker by the entrance, then crank the valve."
msgstr "Węzeł serwisowy przywrócony. Załącz wyłącznik przy wejściu, potem przekręć zawór."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:126
msgid "The service line runs on toward Archive."
msgstr "Linia serwisowa biegnie dalej, do Archiwum."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:129
msgid "The valve is dead. Arm the breaker first."
msgstr "Zawór jest bez zasilania. Najpierw załącz wyłącznik."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:131
msgid ""
"The vent let go and the breaker tripped.\n"
"Reset it by the entrance."
msgstr ""
"Upust puścił, a wyłącznik się wybił.\n"
"Zresetuj go przy wejściu."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:133
msgid ""
"Sealed shut. Something hums behind it.\n"
"The valve beside it charges it."
msgstr ""
"Zamknięte na głucho. Coś za nimi buczy.\n"
"Zawór obok je ładuje."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:135
msgid "Already live. Crank the valve by the door."
msgstr "Już pod ciśnieniem. Kręć zaworem przy drzwiach."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:139
msgid "No charge left. The door is down."
msgstr "Ładunek wyczerpany. Drzwi leżą."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:141
msgid "Not yet. The tank is still going back up."
msgstr "Jeszcze nie. Zbiornik wciąż jedzie do góry."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:143
msgid ""
"The tank is down on the sentry.\n"
"The exit bolt is by the door."
msgstr ""
"Zbiornik leży na strażniku.\n"
"Rygiel wyjścia jest przy drzwiach."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:145
msgid "Locked out until the sentry is down."
msgstr "Zablokowane, dopóki strażnik nie padnie."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:147
msgid "Bolted. The sealed door comes first."
msgstr "Zaryglowane. Najpierw przejdź przez zamknięte drzwi."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:149
msgid "Wait. WOLF hasn't got it on the mark yet."
msgstr "Czekaj. WOLF jeszcze nie ma go na znaczniku."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name, as an object ("for their call"): keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:153
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The door goes. WOLF falls back\n"
"to wait for %s's call."
msgstr ""
"Drzwi puszczają. WOLF cofa się\n"
"i czeka, aż %s da znak."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:155
msgid "Past the doorway, something whirs awake."
msgstr "Za przejściem coś budzi się z warkotem."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the rubble (a button): WOLF draws the sentry under the tank.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:158
msgid "Draw it under the tank if you can stay clear."
msgstr "Ściągnij go pod zbiornik, jeśli możesz trzymać się z dala."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the rubble (a button): the engineer times the drop.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:161
msgid "Stay back, I'll time it."
msgstr "Zostań z tyłu, ja wyczuję moment."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF to the engineer, who told him the relay's risk. Avoid a past tense that shows the engineer's gender ("you told me"): rephrase.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF engineer=you
#: scripts/story_text.gd:164
msgid "You told me the truth at the relay. I'll draw it onto the mark and keep clear of the tank. Drop it when it stops."
msgstr "Przy przekaźniku usłyszałem od ciebie prawdę. Ściągnę go na znacznik i nie wejdę pod zbiornik. Zrzuć go, gdy stanie."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF to the engineer, who pressed him at the relay without warning. Avoid a form that shows the engineer's gender ("you'd have sent me"): rephrase.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF engineer=you
#: scripts/story_text.gd:167
msgid "At the relay you'd have sent me in blind. I won't walk into its sights. Time the drop from the release; it crosses the mark on every pass."
msgstr "Przy przekaźniku przez ciebie poszedłbym w ciemno. Nie wejdę mu na celownik. Wyczuj moment zrzutu przy pulpicie; strażnik mija znacznik przy każdym przejściu."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF, when the engineer will time the drop alone.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:170
msgid ""
"I'll hold back.\n"
"It crosses the mark on every pass."
msgstr ""
"Zostanę z tyłu.\n"
"Strażnik mija znacznik przy każdym przejściu."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:172
msgid "The tank takes a moment to fall."
msgstr "Zbiornik potrzebuje chwili, żeby spaść."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:174
msgid "The sentry stops on the mark, its eyes on WOLF. Drop the tank now."
msgstr "Strażnik staje na znaczniku, wzrok ma na WOLF. Zrzuć zbiornik teraz."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:177
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The sentry stops and its eyes snap red.\n"
"It has %s; get back over the rubble."
msgstr ""
"Strażnik staje, a oczy rozbłyskują mu czerwienią.\n"
"Ma na celowniku: %s; wracaj za gruzowisko."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:180
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The sentry loses %s behind the rubble\n"
"and rolls back to its patrol."
msgstr ""
"Za gruzowiskiem %s znika strażnikowi z oczu,\n"
"a ten wraca do obchodu."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:182
msgid ""
"The tank hits the empty mark\n"
"and sprays coolant."
msgstr ""
"Zbiornik uderza w pusty znacznik\n"
"i rozpryskuje chłodziwo."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:184
msgid ""
"The sentry swings toward the release;\n"
"get back over the rubble."
msgstr ""
"Strażnik obraca się w stronę pulpitu zrzutu;\n"
"wracaj za gruzowisko."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF breaks off after a missed drop, short of the sentry.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:187
msgid "I'm out. I'll hold back."
msgstr "Wycofuję się. Zostanę z tyłu."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF breaks off after a missed drop, already past the sentry.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:190
msgid "I'm out."
msgstr "Wycofuję się."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:192
msgid ""
"The tank comes down square and crushes\n"
"the sentry flat. Its eyes go dark."
msgstr ""
"Zbiornik spada prosto i miażdży\n"
"strażnika na płasko. Jego oczy gasną."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:194
msgid ""
"The tank catches the sentry off centre and\n"
"pins it to the floor. Its eyes go dark."
msgstr "Zbiornik trafia strażnika krzywo i przygważdża go do podłogi. Oczy mu gasną."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:196
msgid "It's down. The bolt by the door is next."
msgstr "Leży. Teraz rygiel przy drzwiach."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:198
msgid "With the tank down, the winch's power reroutes to the exit bolt. The panel whines."
msgstr "Gdy zbiornik leży, zasilanie wciągarki idzie do rygla wyjścia. Panel piszczy."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:202
msgid "The bolt arcs and drops."
msgstr "Rygiel iskrzy i opada."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:204
msgid ""
"The bolt arcs and drops.\n"
"The door slides open."
msgstr ""
"Rygiel iskrzy i opada.\n"
"Drzwi się rozsuwają."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:208
#, c-format
msgid "The relief vent let go under %s. When the gauge peaks, stay off the grate."
msgstr "Wyrzuciło upust ciśnienia, a %s — prosto na kratce. Gdy wskaźnik dojdzie do szczytu, zejdź z kratki."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:211
#, c-format
msgid "The door went with %s in front of it. When the fuse lights, back away past the valve."
msgstr "Drzwi puściły, a %s — tuż przed nimi. Gdy lont się zapali, odsuń się za zawór."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them. TANK RELEASE is a station's name plate.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:214
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The sentry saw %s out in the open.\n"
"Stay close to the TANK RELEASE."
msgstr ""
"Strażnik zauważył: %s na otwartym terenie.\n"
"Trzymaj się blisko „ZRZUT ZBIORNIKA”."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:217
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The sentry ran %s down. Once its\n"
"eyes go red, only the rubble is safe."
msgstr "Strażnik dopadł cel: %s. Gdy oczy strażnika poczerwienieją, bezpieczne jest tylko gruzowisko."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:220
#, c-format
msgid "The coolant cloud caught %s. Let it clear before crossing the mark."
msgstr "W chmurze chłodziwa — %s. Zanim przejdziesz przez znacznik, poczekaj, aż się rozwieje."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
